    "summary": "Indigo gown (boubou, tobe) of very large size, composed of European calico sheeting cut into 20 lengths (these were repeated on both sides of the gown). Each strip was folded along the centre and rope-tied to form a pattern of blue stripes; the ends of each strip were left untied and form a plain dark indigo band along the bottom of the gown. After dyeing the strips were machine-sewn together to form a rectangle, leaving a slit cut in the centre for the wearer’s head. An irregularly shaped small pocket of the same pattern was sewn onto the breast.",
